    <GaugingStation location="Boscadjack" name="Cober" number="48013">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity-area station installed for flood warning purposes in 1998.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Fairly stable shoal forms a natural bed control at lower flows. Has been subject to change but stable since 2011. The site is not bypassed but is impacted by a public water supply abstraction upstream of the site on the River Cober at Trenear gauging station. Between Trenars gauging station and this site, there is a significant input of about 35% of the catchment flow from the Releath Stream. Rated by gaugings to within 75% of bankfull (1.1m) and extrapolated to bank full.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity-area station, about a 4m wide section. Station opened in 1998 as a flood warning level site, one of 3 flow sites on the River Cober. Station added to peak flows dataset in August 2025 (WINFAP Files v14).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">High flow event in 2012 did not change the relationship at high flows.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Moderate influence from public water supply abstraction and compensation flows at Trenear gauging station and industrial abstractions. Flows influenced by hstorical mineworkings in the catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Igneous catchment, granite with some areas of alluvium. Land use is mostly rural/agricultural/ mining with little urbanisation. No major changes to catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff"/>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged to within 70% of bankfull, extrapolated to bankfull." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Not gauged above bankfull." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
